{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1500797-how-do-you-people-prep-your-npc-s-and-opponents","id":1500797,"title":"How do you people prep your NPC's and opponents?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-19T18:01:04-08:00","id":1500797,"title":"How do you people prep your NPC's and opponents?","content":"Looking to run not only my first Werewolf campaign, but my first running of any TTRPG, and I'm getting to a point where I'm making NPC's. So for like Sept members, I'm guessing I don't need to fill out a whole character sheet for them, but what things should I know or have notes of for stats? Similarly with enemies like Black Spiral Dancers: what should I have at the ready? Then there's banes, fomori, and spirits which seem even more complicated.<br /> <br /> I figure everyone has their own styles and methods, and I'm sure I'll develop my own the more I run, but I'd like to at least avoid burning out from unnecessary over prepping.<br /> <br /> Bonus question: I plan on making their first encounter and Rite of Passage assisting a Gurahl in cleansing/healing a small section of a forest that burned over a century ago, but still nothing grows there, even though the area around it had burned as well but has regrown. I'm thinking some sort of leftover smoke bane in the umbra is preventing growth, or tree spirits still angry at being burned. I feel a little stumped (pun might be intended).<br /> <br /> Thanks for your thoughts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4674-ammayhem","name":"AMmayhem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4674_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T18:24:08-08:00","id":1500798,"title":"","content":"So for Septmates and similar NPCs, I typically have<br /> <br /> name, rank, auspice, tribe, a short physical description, a personality write up, and I generally will just write down how many dice I want to roll for various things instead of a precise number per stat. For example, the glass Walker Ahroun Fostern will have 6 or 7 dice in combat rolls, but only 2-4 for some socials, with more for intimidation. I also want to make note of any particular gifts that may come up. <br /> <br /> for black spiral dancers, it depends on the Dancer. If the BSD is an NPC that the characters will have seen and interacted with before, I write them like a Garou NPC as above. Otherwise, I will just write a few personality keywords, and then stat out their combat skills. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bbanes, spirits and fomori are more complicated, you're right! I usually will just take the notes right out of the book in that case, with modified essences as needed. <br /> <br /> for the rite of passage idea, you could have a Smoke bane for sure, who has worked to corrupt the spirits of those trees, so you have corrupted and angry tree spirits attacking and harassing those who try to cleanse the land, hence the Gurahl being awake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27762-jackal-alltrades","name":"Jackal Alltrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T19:40:46-08:00","id":1500802,"title":"","content":"In general my approach is:\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Mooks get as little as I can get away with, generally P/S/M scores from 1-10, Soak value, and standard loadout, if they get prepared stats at all. The vast majority of NPCs are bit parts and don't even need that, you can probably get away with 3 dice for most stuff, 6 for their field of expertise, and one Willpower point of it really becomes important. If I can make mook stats as generic as possible I can reuse them in anything Storyteller-related, which'll save time if I ever need a Sorcerer's Apprentice or Possessed Death Trooper in Scion.<br /> <br /> Minor NPCs and enemies probably get P/S/M scores rated from 1-5, important Abilities and Backgrounds, and a basic equipment list. If it becomes important they c\u00e0n spend up to two Rage/Willpower/Gnosis per scene The deciding point when prepping for a session is 'do they have a name', throwaways who become important can have a basic sheet put together. More importance means more detail, including defined Gifts/Numina/other powers, until we reach level three. If a Garou is unimportant enough they might not get a defined Auspice or Tribe until the players ask.<br /> <br /> Werewolf, Fomori, and similar opponents are probably not worth being mooks, but probably don't need much in the way of actual stats. You can probably get away with picking Gifts to make a fun encounter rather than worrying about what makes sense.<br /> <br /> NPCs and enemies get full sheets if and when I like them enough to make them. This means they're intended to be recurring (although I've stopped using plot armour), they're probably intended to engage in a lot of situations, and I haven't been distracted by something shiny. This is maybe a handful of characters in a half year Chronicle, and probably not many more if I ever run anything longer.<br /> <br /> As for Spirits and Banes? Honestly you can still probably use the same idea, although as Spirits only have three stats anyway (Rage/Willpower/Gnosis). Mostly what'll help is being willing to add and remove Charms on the fly when you realise your spirit really should be able to do this but you forgot to put the dang thing on there. But you can probably get away with just not starting minor spirits most of the time, so your your Rite of Passage you probably need a Smoke Bane, a generic Tree spirit, and any other Spirits you think will be fun to add (maybe some sort of insect spirit which used to feed on the dead plants and dropped leaves, just as important a part of the forest as the trees themselves).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T20:14:38-08:00","id":1500806,"title":"","content":"I try to keep it as simple as possible. Most NPCs start out as generic. Stats tend to be &quot;dice pool size&quot;. &quot;6 dice for combat&quot; &quot;4 dice for mental&quot; &quot;3 dice for social&quot; and the same Gifts for certain types of characters. Some NPCs are combat NPCs, others are support NPCs, and others are leaders. So I might only have 3 to 5 &quot;styles&quot; of generic NPCs. For Ranks, add 1 extra dice to one of the pools of your choice for each rank. And feel fry to change things on the fly for a specific individual when needed. Not every character with a 4 dice pool for mental stuff will be able to do everything, so it's OK to say that NPC doesn't know how to lockpick, but I will give him 2 more dice for computer. Or whatever.<br /> <br /> Only as individual NPCs become important to the game (based on what the PCs do) do they start getting customized stats that I record based on the needs of the game.<br /> <br /> I also use the &quot;index card rule&quot;. I try to keep everything I need for that NPC on one index card. I now try to avoid creating an entire character sheet as I found I don't need 80%. As I begin to customize an NPC from the generic stuff, I can quickly make notes on the index card and write a name.<br /> <br /> It works well enough most of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T04:14:53-08:00","id":1500916,"title":"","content":"If it's an important character they're going to have a writeup with some character traits, allegiances, quirks and plot relevant needs and plans. Occasionally a plot relevant rite or gift might be noted just because it'd be cool to showcase or as a problem for the protagonists. Outside that they don't need proper stats. It's easy to judge what their role in the story is and give them dicepoools and health levels based on that. Making full sheets is just a waste of time and unnecessary as the NPC's don't need to follow same generation rules as the PC's.<br /> <br /> I go with the following:<br /> <br /> Mooks - 5 dice to relevant pools, 3 HL<br /> Elites - 7 dice to relevant pools, 7HL<br /> Antagonists - 8-10 dice to relevant pools, 7HL (or a few extra if needed)<br /> <br /> Spirits and certain monsters might be a bit more complicated, but you can solve most NPC needs with these guys (including a large variety of those two). If they ever need a dicpool for a skill they're not good at, I just halve their relevant dicepool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}